# Python helper index

Before designing or reviewing a reusable infrastructure helper or its caller, match the need
below and read its design rule. Read the implementation template only when adding, adapting,
or reviewing the helper itself. Use only rows whose design rule is installed in the target
repository.

| Need | Existing helper | Design | Implementation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Finite persisted lifecycle with a meaningful transition graph | `StateMachine` / `AsyncStateMachine` | [`python-fsm.mdc`](../python-fsm/python-fsm.mdc) | [`FSM.md`](../python-fsm/FSM.md) |
| Smallest independently repeatable transient adapter operation; idempotent writes and per-attempt timeout | `retry_on_exception` / `retry_unless_exception` | [`python-retry.mdc`](../python-retry/python-retry.mdc) | [`RETRY.md`](../python-retry/RETRY.md) |
| Outbound HTTP adapter using the developer-selected async or sync client | `AsyncApi` / `SyncApi` | [`python-base-client.mdc`](../python-base-client/python-base-client.mdc) | [`ASYNC_CLIENT.md`](../python-base-client/ASYNC_CLIENT.md) or [`SYNC_CLIENT.md`](../python-base-client/SYNC_CLIENT.md) |

Use ordinary conditionals for independent flags or lifecycles without a meaningful transition
graph.
